  "title": "Provider-neutral harness seam and the dsh adapter",
  "summary": "Adds a provider-neutral `harness` module (the `Harness`/`CommandRunner` traits, `CommandSpec`, `HarnessResult`, capability reporting, prompt and question-line helpers) plus in-memory fakes, and the first concrete adapter, `dsh_harness`, which drives `dsh --profile headless --json -` through a `CommandRunner`, parses its newline-delimited JSON events, and brackets each run with `git status`/`rev-parse` checks. The adapter never starts a process itself: it builds `CommandSpec`s, and the runner executes them. A run is rejected before the agent starts if the tree is dirty, and fails afterwards if the turn ended with a non-`completed` reason, if no final event was printed, or if the agent moved HEAD.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
